Subject: engine: parking a plain object takes the direct route to the deferred list

What this does
  js_drc_zero parks a value whose reference count reached zero. For an object of class
  JS_CLASS_OBJECT it now links the object onto the deferred list directly, without the tag switch
  and without the large-value walk. Both are still there for every other value, and a plain object
  can never be one the large-value walk names: it has no string, rope, BigInt, array buffer, typed
  array or data view of its own.

Why we need it
  A plain object is the common counted value: tree reaches js_drc_zero 2,948,676 times for
  1,474,039 frees, and the tag switch plus the large-value switch is paid on every one of those
  parks. The two tests the shortcut skips are a class-id compare and a tag compare on the fast
  path, and the switch table's code is what the profile attributes to the site.

Hazards
  The parked object is marked in_zct and counted in zct_nobj exactly as before, so a borrowing
  register that still names it is validated the same way, and reconcile's keep-or-free decision is
  unchanged. Weak references, finalizers and FinalizationRegistry never see this path: a plain
  object of class JS_CLASS_OBJECT has no class finalizer, and a weak reference or a
  FinalizationRegistry entry is not a class of its own, so the object still goes through
  free_object and reset_weak_ref as before when reconcile frees it.

Tests: .local/tests/alloc-free-plain.js and tests/differential/corpus/alloc-free-plain.js (asan,
AOT and interpreter arms equal to node); tree, raytrace, deltablue, closure and richards outputs
equal to the interpreter.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -10603,6 +10603,19 @@
         js_free_value_rt(rt, v);
         return;
     }
+    if (likely(tag == JS_TAG_OBJECT)) {
+        JSGCObjectHeader *p = JS_VALUE_GET_PTR(v);
+        if (likely(((JSObject *)p)->class_id == JS_CLASS_OBJECT)) {
+            /* A plain object is not a value js_drc_value_is_large() can call
+               large, so parking it takes neither the tag switch below nor the
+               large-value walk. */
+            list_del(&p->link);
+            list_add(&p->link, &rt->gc_zero_ref_count_list);
+            JS_GC_IN_ZCT(p) = 1;
+            rt->zct_nobj++;
+            return;
+        }
+    }
     if (js_drc_value_is_large(v)) {
         /* One large value can dominate the parked memory before allocation
            pressure is even felt; make the next safepoint reconcile. */
